    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d735">

                <pb facs="0838" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.21/478: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Philip</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-05T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Confidential. Your 108, August 2, 3 p.m., received early August 5th<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d735-f1"/> and immediately communicated to Senator Lodge.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d735-f1" n="15" xml:id="d735-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram of Aug. 2 received in the Department’s telegraph office on Aug. 4 at
                    4.30 p.m., but was not distributed in the Department until the following
                    morning.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
